From 7129ebba1836e19f941b9b274fd5565a66c1106d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 19:13:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07701/11362] [outer-loop] ARC perception fix: HUD-register +
 mover/entity detectors (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5833)

Builds the perception fix the oracle-perception ablation (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5832)
justified. Two detectors, both from the agent's OWN transitions (oracle-distinct,
no source-reading):
  - detect_hud_registers: edge bands whose cell count changes monotonically on
    most actions = a status counter (fill/deplete) to ignore. Distinguishes a
    counter from the interactive board via monotone_ratio + changed_fraction.
  - detect_mover: the color whose centroid translates with directional actions
    (1-4) = the player.
perceive_entities composes them into the detector-produced analogue of 5832's
hand-authored oracle facts (entity presence/role only, never the goal).

9 unit tests (synthetic frames with a known HUD band + known mover), ruff+mypy clean.
Next: integration gate re-running the 5832 goal measurement under detector-produced
perception on real game transitions.

